{"type": "text", "text": "QA sweep of **Iris Gallery** completed (the device session was terminated before I could restore all test data or sign off).\n\n## Bug confirmed by developer\n**Media tab – Videos blank state caption is wrong**\n- Path: Media tab → Filter → Videos (0)\n- Shown: `No photos found`\n- Expected: `No videos found`\n- Developer reply: *“thanks, confirmed and logged.”*\n\n## Additional issue filed (no developer reply received)\n**A remaining photo disappears from Media/Albums after a delete**\n- Start: Media has 6 photos, including `big (1).jpg`.\n- Delete `huge.jpg`; the viewer filmstrip correctly shows the remaining 5 (including `big (1).jpg`).\n- Return to Media: only 4 tiles are shown — `big (1).jpg` is missing.\n- Albums also drops the Beta album containing it, and it is not in Trash (Trash contains only `huge.jpg`).\n- It reappears only after a later restore/refresh operation, so this is a list-refresh/consistency defect rather than real data loss.\n\n## Other observations reported but rejected\n- Album grid showed duplicate same-name album cards (two `IrisSeed`, later two `Beta`) after photo restores.\n- Single-item counts display `1 items` instead of `1 item`.\n- In landscape, albums on the second grid row are overlapped by the floating bottom navigation bar, hiding their names/counts; the grid does not scroll them into view.\n\n## Data state at end of session\nTesting intentionally used the Trash workflow. `IrisSeed/huge.jpg` was left in Trash, and `Beta/big (1).jpg` was temporarily absent from the Media/Albums lists when the session ended. The precondition album IrisSeed was therefore left in a non-standard state."}
